{
  "title": "RAW manuscript constraint: Galen NOT synonyms conflict with a newly assumed symmetric r/l involution",
  "summary": "RAW_UNREVIEWED_NOT_EXECUTED. Actual parent499/501 words supply or=NOT, ol=TO, sol=NOT and sor=MUCH. A new context-free symmetric meaning-level r/l toggle would demand T(NOT)=TO from or→ol and T(NOT)=MUCH from sol→sor. The directions are opposite. This is an explicit conditional counterexample to that added operator plus the unchanged meanings; it is not a contradiction of one directed r→l function, not a result of915/916, and not a corpus experiment. Complete source-bound parent paragraphs and full lexicon entries retained.",
  "scope": "semantic",
  "status": "RAW_UNREVIEWED_CONDITIONAL_WORD_COMPOSITION_COUNTERCASE_NOT_EXECUTED",
  "created_utc": "2026-09-22T09:41:12.537190+00:00",
  "design": {
    "mechanism": "One deterministic extensional involution T interprets the terminal r/l switch in both directions on the complete uninstantiated word denotation.",
    "unit": "Exactly the observed whole-word pairs or/ol and sol/sor in the two existing complete Galen hypotheses.",
    "contrast": "One symmetric T versus separate directed functions R_to_L and L_to_R, or a function carrying explicit lexeme/terminal-state identity.",
    "prediction": "The symmetric contract must give the identical NOT denotation one result. The unchanged TO and MUCH outputs have incompatible declared types, so the two requirements cannot both hold.",
    "scope": "New narrowly declared compositional hypothesis with a visible countercase; no general r/l meaning or new-stem transfer claim."
  },
